spec:
  grid: 8-16 rows x 8-16 cols, square [observed]
  background: 7 (orange) [observed]; must be most frequent color
  corner_objects:
    count: 3-4, each anchored at a distinct grid corner (bbox touches both borders forming that corner)
    bbox: 1-4 rows x 1-4 cols; must include the corner pixel itself
    pixels: 2-12; density 0.62-1.0 (most are fully filled rectangles)
    color: monochromatic, non-background; colors may repeat across corners
    constraint: for adjacent occupied corners on same edge, sum of their extent along that edge < grid dimension (ensures stamps don't overlap)
  distractors:
    count: 4-14 (scales with grid size); small monochromatic 4-connected blobs
    bbox: 1-5 rows x 1-4 cols; pixels 1-5
    placement: scattered in grid interior or touching at most one border (never two adjacent borders forming a corner)
    colors: may share colors with corner objects or each other
  rule: |
    Copy each corner-anchored object clockwise to the next corner (TL->TR, TR->BR, BR->BL, BL->TL).
    Orientation is preserved; the copy's bbox is aligned to the destination corner.
    Copies overwrite whatever is underneath (including existing corner objects).
    Source objects remain in place.

generation_strategy:
